  "summary_en": "Swiss Federal Council ordinance (in force 1 March 2025) regulating approval and use of motor vehicles with automation systems: takeover-request vehicles (motorway), automated parking and driverless vehicles. Sets technical requirements, type approval aligned with UNECE/EU rules, data recorders, cybersecurity, incident reporting, remote operators, and penalties.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Automation systems and vehicles require type approval, aligned with UNECE and EU Regulation 2022/1426; no exemptions.",
   "Vehicles must carry a driving-mode data recorder; data use limited to expert reports and accident/criminal investigations.",
   "Manufacturers need UN R155 cybersecurity and R156 software update management certificates.",
   "Driverless vehicles must be supervised by a trained natural-person operator located in Switzerland; cantons approve operating areas.",
   "Manufacturers/importers must report safety-relevant incidents to ASTRA, which can demand software and training data access and suspend approvals."
  ],
